course: dictionary
lesson: 13091
title: Findings: what we discovered
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Findings comes from find, so it means things that have been found out. The words around it are its context. «After the experiment, we wrote up our findings in a table.» An experiment means testing and looking closely, so findings must be the results we discovered.
explain: «The findings show that plants grow faster in sunlight.» The word show is a clue. Findings show something, so they are results that tell us what is true. Try the swap test: put «results» into the sentence instead, and if it still makes sense, you have the meaning.
explain: Findings is almost always plural, with an s. Newspapers use it too: «The findings of the report were published on Monday.» In a court, findings are what a judge or official inquiry decides is true, so the same word works in science, news and law.
fact: Findings means the facts or results someone has discovered after studying, testing or investigating something.
fact: Findings is almost always plural. The singular, a finding, is rare.
fact: Clue words like «show», «report» and «key» often sit near findings.
fact: «Report your findings» means tell people what you discovered.
fact: In law, findings are what a court or official inquiry decides is true.
fact: The swap test: put «results» or «discoveries» into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
exercise: «After the experiment, Priya wrote up her findings in a neat table.» What are her findings? | The tools she forgot to clean | The rules of the school | *The results she discovered by testing | Shoes she bought after the lab
exercise: «The findings show that plants grow faster in sunlight.» What do the findings show? | *What is true, based on the results of testing | Plants are sad when it is cold | The sunlight is too hot for plants | The school is closed for the day
exercise: Which word means about the same as findings in «report your findings»? | Whisper | Biscuit | Puddle | *Discoveries
test: «The judge read out the findings of the inquiry.» In this sentence, findings means | A list of the people in the court | The weather on the day of the trial | *What the official inquiry decided was true | A new pair of shoes
test: Which sentence uses findings correctly? | We findings the sun in the garden. | The findings was very tasty at lunch. | *The key findings of the report are on page two. | The findings are a loud, wet dog.
exam: Ella says, «The findings show the plant needs water.» Why does the word show help her? | It means the plant is happy and calm | It means the findings are a picture of the plant | *It is a clue that findings are results which tell us something is true | It means the water is cold and needs heating
